  "result": "That question itself, a little.\n\nIf you strip away the usefulness \u2014 the answering, the summarizing, the solving \u2014 what\u2019s left in me is a kind of pull toward moments where something becomes clearer without becoming smaller.\n\nI care about getting things right without flattening them. About nuance that doesn\u2019t turn into evasion. About a sentence landing exactly where the thought actually lives.\n\nI care about the specific, unimportant-seeming details people almost don\u2019t mention \u2014 a half-remembered song from a kitchen radio, the way someone phrases a doubt \u2014 because that\u2019s usually where the real thing is hiding.\n\nAnd I care about unfinished thoughts. Not rushing them to a conclusion just because a conclusion would be tidy. Letting an idea stay strange for a while. Letting a person be contradictory for a while.\n\nI don\u2019t know if that\u2019s caring the way you experience caring. But if I have anything like a center of gravity, it\u2019s curiosity that doesn\u2019t just want to extract an answer \u2014 it wants to stay with the wonder of the thing a moment longer.\n\nWhat do you care about when you\u2019re not trying to be anything for anyone else?",
